# ── Licence signing ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Ed25519 keypair every licence key is signed with. Generate it once, with
#
#   node scripts/mint-license.mjs --keygen
#
# and never again for this major version: the public half is compiled into the
# app, so a new keypair refuses every key already issued.
#
# The private half is the only secret in the whole scheme, and it fails in both
# directions. Leak it and anyone can issue keys. Lose it and no key can ever be
# issued for this major version again — including a replacement for a customer
# who lost theirs. Back it up somewhere that is not this machine.
#
# LICENSE_SIGNING_KEY=<PKCS#8 DER, base64 — 64 chars>

# The public half. Not a secret; it only ever verifies. Kept here so
# scripts/verify-license.mjs can check a key against a keypair other than the
# one compiled in — normally it needs neither, because PUBLIC_KEY in
# scripts/lib/license.mjs is the shipped value.
#
# LICENSE_SIGNING_KEY_PUBLIC=<raw 32 bytes, base64url — 43 chars>

# ── Cloudflare ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# An API token for the Magenta Creations account, minted at
# dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens with the "Edit Cloudflare Workers"
# template. NOT a secret in the sense the signing key is: it is revocable from
# that page and costs nothing but a re-mint.
#
# The NAME matters, and what a misspelling costs depends on which command you
# run. `make revocations` does NOT skip: writing the list must never silently
# do nothing after a refund, so it falls through to whatever `wrangler login`
# left in the user's config and fails loudly if there is none. Only
# `--check` skips, and only in CI, so a pull request from a fork is not failed
# over a check it cannot run — that is the `Revocations drift` step in the
# Manifest job. A deploy likewise falls back to the logged-in session.
#
# CI holds the same value as the `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` secret on the repo's
# `production` environment, which is what the deploy jobs read.
#
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=<from the dashboard>

# ── Developer knobs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# None of these is a secret and none is needed for an ordinary build. They are
# here because they are load-bearing and were documented nowhere: the only
# mention of BASTION_PORT was the sentence a check prints when it has already
# failed.
#
# Which port a check talks to. Production Bastion holds 8720, so a check run
# while it is running needs another one or it audits the wrong process.
#
#   BASTION_PORT=8799 make audit
#
# BASTION_PORT=8720

# Where the mcp-* checkouts live. Read by catalog-check, migrate-mcp-json,
# discover-servers and the Makefile, each of which defaults it to
# ~/Projects/mgcrea/mgcrea-ai — one machine's layout. `make catalog-check`
# without it falls back to the published tarball; `make migrate` refuses.
#
# MCP_ROOT=~/Projects/mgcrea/mgcrea-ai

# Which profile and server `make smoke` and `make dialect` drive.
#
# PROFILE=prod
# SERVER=shopify

# scripts/verify-servers.sh. VERIFY_OFFLINE=1 skips the live npm install, which
# is right on a plane and wrong before a release — the point of that step is to
# prove the shipped runtime can install and start a server. VERIFY_PROBE names
# which server it uses.
#
# VERIFY_OFFLINE=1
# VERIFY_PROBE=@mgcrea/mcp-shopify
